A||N||2||Lewis||Starting problem...after I run the car>>||||5||
Z||000000||Lewis||06-24-2000||12:03 PM||||I have a 85GT and after driving the car for awhile it is hard to start actually it will not start right away.  Have to wait for 1/2 hour or so.  When I try to crank it after turning it off it is as though the battery is going dead.  Called a local shop and he told me to jump it when it does this if it starts it is a battery problem but it will not turn over even with a jump.  I replace the selinoid a few months ago.  Could it be a starter problem and how can I make sure it is or not.  I can remove the starter and take it to the shop to be tested but I would rather know if it could be another problem before I do that.  Replace plugs and distributor and rotor already.  I think the key point here is the sound the car makes when trying to restart it.  The sound is just like a low battery where it just whines down and is barely turning the starter.  Any suggestions would be appreciated.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||06-24-2000||12:22 PM||||It's the starter that is bad. Usually when they get old and hot they won't start. Odds are if you remove it to have it tested and it has cooled off it'll work. This is a common problem with a lot of GM cars.||||reg||1
Z||000002||N_Man||06-24-2000||06:52 PM||||If your solinoid is still good get a starter rebuild kit.<P>My started used to make a horrible noise got the rebuild kit.  It came with new brushes and bushings.  Now it is smooth.||||reg||1
